# Presentation-golden corpus manifest for Spyro 2 (fields as in
# games/spyro-1/corpus/presentation-corpus.manifest: name|start|interval|freeze|pins).
#
# attract-demo has no bk2: the row is the plain boot, the title screen and the
# attract demo, which need no input. A movie-less row takes its length from its
# last pin, so every frame it wants is pinned.
#
# The pins are the demo's level-loaded stretches, read off the native terrain
# feed's per-present triangle count over a 19583-VBL boot. The count holds at
# 1985 between segments (the title-screen world) and departs from it while a
# demo level is resident: 3304-3722, 3726-4358, 6450-7774, 9866-11684,
# 13776-15316 and 17408-18558. Each pin sits inside one of those stretches,
# clear of its load transient, so the row covers five distinct levels of world
# geometry and texture data. The grid samples between them hold the
# title-screen world.
# 4358 is a camera cut: the demo's second segment ends with the camera stepping
# 98094 world units in one tick, with every drawn record carrying a previous
# tick of its own. The intermediate leg there shows the previous tick for the
# whole interval; the canonical leg is unaffected.
# 1273 and 1973 are the title screen: the logo sprite and the "press start"
# text, linked into the ordering table at an explicit depth slot
# (func_8001B354) rather than at the head (func_8001B390); pinned for the
# slotted-insert hook. Pins below start are unioned with the grid.
# 1057 is the boot scene before the title: under --lod extended the distant
# low-poly spires between the left cliffs and the skull do not draw, where
# --lod original and the guest reference draw them (64533 px differ).
attract-demo|3973|3000||1057,1273,1973,3973,4358,7073,10773,14573,17973
# attract-demo@heldfade: a present of the held-fade loop after the entry at
# 3232 (isbg=0, one subtractive quad per VBL over the held picture).
attract-demo@heldfade|3234|100|freeze|3236
#
# autumn-plains-skelos-badlands-portal-entry: a portal entry from the home
# world, the in-gameplay level change. 1723 is the portal transition, 1823 and
# 1923 the flight with the treasure tally, 2123 the flight with the level name,
# 2273 the arrival cutscene in the entered level.
# 1646, 1658, 1712 and 1774 are the transition's quiet regime edges: the ticks
# where g_GameState steps -1 -> 0 -> 1 -> 2 and 6 -> 7, each stepping the
# camera by at most 116 world units, three orders under the cut guard's
# position threshold and inside its rotation threshold. The pair across such an
# edge spans two simulation regimes rather than one motion, so the
# intermediate leg holds the previous tick instead of lerping the chord; the
# canonical leg is unaffected.
autumn-plains-skelos-badlands-portal-entry|1723|200||1423,1424,1425,1646,1658,1712,1723,1774,1823,1923,2123,2273
# @tcache / @tcsqueeze: the retained terrain cache forced on (llvmpipe refuses it
# otherwise) across a level edge; @tcsqueeze also sizes every arena primary at
# 32768 elements (OPENPETE_TC_INITIAL_CAP) so the arenas grow mid-level. Coverage
# rows of the arena-growth path: the image must match the unsqueezed run.
autumn-plains-skelos-badlands-portal-entry@tcache|1723|200||1723,2273|OPENPETE_TERRAIN_CACHE_FORCE=1
autumn-plains-skelos-badlands-portal-entry@tcsqueeze|1723|200||1723,2273|OPENPETE_TERRAIN_CACHE_FORCE=1 OPENPETE_TC_INITIAL_CAP=32768
#
# colossus-ice-skating: the player on the Colossus rink with the mirrored copy
# under the ice. 1494, 1694 and 1734 are intermediate legs whose tick pair spans a
# body keyframe advance; 1696 is the leg after one.
colossus-ice-skating|1473|200||1494,1503,1694,1696,1734
# colossus-ice-skating@wall: the player beside the rink's wall, VBL 1886;
# native draws the mirrored copy's tail and horns but not its body under
# the player, which the guest draws. Blessed pre-fix.
colossus-ice-skating@wall|1886|200||1886

# summer-forest-collect-orb: the orb pickup with the 3D orb HUD icon at the
# bottom edge. 1455 is the reported tick where the guest frames the orb icon
# with four golden facets and the native draws the orb alone; 1443 and 1467
# bracket it. The bk2 is 1457 frames, so the grid stops at 1459.
summer-forest-collect-orb|1455|2||1443,1455,1467
#
# shady-oasis-flame: two flame breaths in Shady Oasis. The flame's primitives
# are written at VBL 1415-1431 (peak 1419) and 1533-1549 (peak 1537); 1421 is an
# intermediate leg inside the first breath.
shady-oasis-flame|1413|200||1419,1421,1423,1537
#
# flame-charge: a flame breath in Autumn Plains followed at once by a charge,
# with the breath's smoke puffs on screen through the charge. Over VBL
# 1433-1479 the particle routine stamps class-0 records whose ordering key
# (SZ3 >> 5) - size - 2 is not positive and then appends no primitive for
# them (partsdraw.s:745, :753), up to 8 per tick. 1449 and 1450 are ticks with
# such records; 1430 and 1466 bracket the stretch, 1434 opens it.
flame-charge|1425|25||1430,1434,1449,1450,1466
#
# open-pause-menu: the pause menu open over Summer Forest, 1473 and 1491. The
# menu box is an opaque flat quad under ten tiled panels, a frame and six
# rows of sprite text; the guidebook page beside it carries quad-form glyphs
# (the level banner, the two gem-row slashes).
open-pause-menu|1473|200||1473,1491
#
# open-guidebook: the guidebook open on its contents page, 1553 and 1571. The
# right-hand column (entry names, placeholder dashes, per-cent signs) is
# quad-form glyph text; the digits are sprite text.
open-guidebook|1533|200||1553,1571
#
# glimmer-pogo-dialogue: the first dialogue in Glimmer. At 1573 the large
# semi-transparent text box and the speaker's name box are both open; the
# large box's four corners are the stepped corner pieces. 1273 is the title
# fly-in before the level, where the game's logo slides in at the top.
# 1470, 1474 and 1476 straddle Pogo's blend from anim 0 into anim 3 (the id
# changes at 1476); 1560 and 1562 straddle two NPCs' blend from anim 0 into
# anim 1: the intermediate legs show whether the sub-tick pose is continuous
# across a tick while the game blends toward the next animation.
glimmer-pogo-dialogue|1473|200||1273,1470,1474,1476,1560,1562,1573
# Pause menu mid-level: the framebuffer window copies draw buffer 0 at VBL
# 2042 and shrinks over 2027-2042 from full screen to the lower-left
# quarter; pins at the first full-window frame, mid-shrink and settled.
# Synthesized: idle to 2023 then Start (make_bk2.py --hold 2023:2033:Start).
pause-menu-midlevel|2013|200||2027,2035,2073
# pause-menu-midlevel@shrink: the same movie pinned on every VBL of the shrink and the
# settle (one game tick per VBL): the window must show the scaled image of
# the tick being drawn, not the first shrink tick's scene. Blessed pre-fix.
pause-menu-midlevel@shrink|2013|200||2027,2028,2029,2030,2031,2032,2033,2034,2035,2036,2037,2038,2039,2040,2041,2042,2043,2044,2045,2046,2047,2048,2049
# pause-menu-midlevel@shrink-freeze: the first shrink steps with the frozen-world
# backdrop, so the 16:9 side strips show whether the window's border stays inside
# the 4:3 window (without the backdrop the strips are black and hide it).
pause-menu-midlevel@shrink-freeze|2013|200|freeze|2027,2028,2029
# pause-unpause: Start again at 2173; the game grows the window back over
# 2190-2197 from the other draw buffer, then draws the live world. Blessed
# pre-fix. 2192 is the first grow step after the draw buffer's image is
# stored: its cells were fed in texel space at 2191 and in image pixels at
# 2192, and the intermediate leg shows whether they pair across that change
# (the window between the 9/16 and 10/16 boxes) or stand at 10/16.
pause-unpause|2173|200||2189,2191,2192,2193,2195,2197,2199
# colour-cheat-red: the pause-menu colour cheat (Up Right Down Left Up Square
# R1 R2 L1 L2 Up Left Down Right Up, then Circle) sets D_800698CC to 1, and
# from VBL 2328 on the tick writer stores 0xA0000090 at g_Spyro+0x20: the player
# draw cues the model colour table toward far colour (0x90, 0, 0) at IR0 0xA00.
colour-cheat-red|2400|100||2400,2401,2500,2600
# credits-cheat: the pause-menu credits cheat from Summer Forest (Square,
# Circle x3, then Left, Right x3) reaches the credits at VBL 2264. 3678 and
# 4572 are sub-tick presents with credits letters flying in and departing:
# the draw compacts the CreditsLetter records in states 1-3 into consecutive
# moby slots, so a departing or reused record moves every later letter to
# another slot.
credits-cheat|2300|200||3678,4572
#
# start-new-game: same-moby self-interpenetration. Two faces of one
# moby that cross in 3D show their crossing contour under true depth, where
# the PSX paints each face whole in OT order; the same-moby rank applies the
# game's paint order between such faces only. At 665 a pink sliver shows
# through a near dark shape. Start 1043 (the movie is 1046 VBLs) keeps the grid
# to two samples.
start-new-game|1043|10||665
# intro cutscene, VBL 1667: one of the sheep's eyes is covered by its own
# face geometry (native); the guest draws the eye.
intro-sheep-eye|1657|10||1667|--skip-to-cutscene intro
# intro cutscene, VBL 2170-2178 at 16:9: on intermediate presents the static
# tree moby on the left leaves the screen and returns.
intro-tree-subtick|2170|2||2170,2172,2173,2174,2175,2176,2178|--skip-to-cutscene intro
# intro_arrival cutscene, VBL 1703-1719: a face of the left green wall gem
# flickers as the camera moves, the gem and the wall it is set into trading
# visibility at the gem's outline (native); the guest's outline is steady.
intro-arrival-gem|1701|2||1709,1710,1711,1712,1713|--skip-to-cutscene intro_arrival
# intro_arrival cutscene, VBL 1983-1989: the base of the portal moby slides
# against the ground terrain from tick to tick (native).
intro-arrival-portal-base|1979|2||1983,1984,1985,1986,1987,1988,1989|--skip-to-cutscene intro_arrival
# intro cutscene at 32:9, VBL 1595-1599: two terrain faces at the far right
# of the frame do not draw (native).
intro-32x9-farright|1591|2||1595,1597,1599|--skip-to-cutscene intro --aspect 32:9
# intro_arrival cutscene, VBL 5829-5833: the roof of Ripto's mouth speckles
# dark through its red face (native); the guest draws it clean.
intro-arrival-ripto-mouth|5823|2||5829,5831,5833|--skip-to-cutscene intro_arrival
# crush_intro cutscene, VBL 1585: orb geometry stretches across the screen
# on the sub-tick view (native); the canonical tick draws clean.
crush-intro-orb-stretch|1577|2||1583,1584,1585,1586,1587|--skip-to-cutscene crush_intro
# crush_intro cutscene, VBL 2176: on a camera cut the mobys vanish for a
# moment on the sub-tick view (native); the canonical ticks draw them.
crush-intro-cut-mobys|2170|2||2174,2175,2176,2177,2178|--skip-to-cutscene crush_intro
# summer_forest cutscene, VBL 1912-1922: Moneybags (class 5, moby 800e7d80)
# falls toward the dome on track segments of 0x800 world units or more, which
# the sampler places in one tick after a tick at rest; the sub-tick view holds
# each such step as a jump (native), so at 1914, 1918 and 1922 the
# intermediate leg shows the previous tick whole while the banners lerp. 1912
# is the last sixteenth-step interval before the first placed segment.
summer-forest-moneybags-fall|1910|2||1912,1914,1916,1918,1920,1922|--skip-to-cutscene summer_forest
# attract-demo-spawn-jump: a class 0x1e3 moby placed without a marker the
# native path reads (named residual); the sub-tick view lerps across it.
# Blessed pre-fix.
attract-demo-spawn-jump|14612|2||14614,14615,14616,14617,14618
# glimmer-32x9-leftedge: the reported free-camera pose at 32:9; the terrain
# occlusion cull's frustum half bounded each sector's sphere with a square
# box too small off-axis and culled sector 69 at the left edge (pink
# background). Blessed on the headless-occlusion build, before the fix.
glimmer-32x9-leftedge|2471|2||2473|--skip-to-level glimmer --aspect 32:9 OPENPETE_FREECAM_POSE=30338,87973,7965,-194,52
#
# s2-create-save: a new game on a blank card in slot 1 (provisioned formatted
# by the binary in the leg's directory) creates and writes its save. 1022
# ("Accessing MEMORY CARDS") and 1104 ("Creating save block") are presents
# where the game draws nothing: the display shows the last image drawn into
# the buffer it shows, the world under the card box.
s2-create-save|1022|82||1022,1104|--card1 {legdir}/card1.mcr --no-card2
#
# idol-springs-level-entry: the level entry from Summer Forest into Idol
# Springs, ending on the loading screen's treasure tally (VBL ~2960-3460; the
# gems fly 2980-3160). The movie ends at 2596 and the row samples the game
# running on without input. In builder state 2 (D_800698F0) the loading
# overlay rebuilds the moby array every tick: one class-1 moby per active
# tally record (*D_80067110, stride 8, active byte +4), then the counter gem
# (+0x0C 0x154, +0x14 0xC00), then the total gem (+0x0C 0xB4). 3060 and 3120
# are sub-tick presents with gems in flight: a spawn or a landing moves every
# later gem to another slot.
idol-springs-level-entry|3000|200||3060,3120
# Cutscene letterbox bars growing 2 PSX rows per tick (VBL 1413-1435): the
# intermediate leg must show them between the two ticks. Blessed pre-fix.
riptos_arena-letterbox|1413|2||1415,1425|--skip-to-level riptos_arena
# settings-menu: the settings menu (OPENPETE_MENU_DEMO opens it at boot)
# drawn into the capture by --screenshot-overlays, over summer_forest. Its text is
# the credits font's glyph models, read from WAD.WAD on the disc
# (text_moby.c, GAME_FONT_WAD_MODEL).
settings-menu|2073|100||2073|--skip-to-level summer_forest OPENPETE_MENU_DEMO=1 --screenshot-overlays
# crushs-dungeon (games/spyro-2/bk2/crushs-dungeon.bk2): the floor's far lip
# loses the terrain key contest to the lava behind it under --lod extended
# (per-cell keys on pinned far faces); 1506 is the sub-tick present the
# reporter saw. Blessed pre-fix.
crushs-dungeon|1504|2||1504,1506
